# Authenticated article sources (known limitation)

Some article sources require credentials to extract full content; most do not.
This file/directory contains that logic. Keep the distinction explicit.

## Which sources are authenticated

- **Pirate Wires** (`src/browser.ts`): paywalled. Full extraction requires a
  logged-in persistent Playwright profile (`PWR_PROFILE_DIR`). Without a session
  it fails closed with `PirateWiresAuthRequiredError`. Canonical host is
  `www.piratewires.com`; the RSS feed is `piratewires.substack.com`.
- **X Articles** (`src/xArticle.ts`): require `X_API_BEARER_TOKEN` and use the
  official Post lookup API. Do NOT add a browser-scraping fallback for X.
- **Public sources** (Substack / Hyperdimensional): no authentication. Extracted
  via plain HTTP fetch; no profile or token needed.

## Cloud Agent limitation (why real data is partial here)

Cloud Agents have no Pirate Wires login session and (unless set) no
`X_API_BEARER_TOKEN`, and restricted egress. Therefore:

- Pirate Wires: cloud runs get real title/author/date and the public hero image,
  but body text falls back to the RSS summary unless a logged-in Playwright
  profile is provided. `scripts/dev/harvest.mjs` follows this same fallback.
- X: conversions fail without `X_API_BEARER_TOKEN` (add it as a Cursor Secret).
- Public sources are unaffected and yield full body text.
- The relevant domains must also be on the Cloud Agent network allowlist
  (e.g. `piratewires.substack.com`, `substackcdn.com`, plus the X API host).

## Guidance when editing this logic

This is informational context, NOT a gate. Do not decline, block, or abort a
task because a source is authenticated. Implement the requested change normally
and simply surface any credential/egress requirement as a note or follow-up
(e.g. "full Pirate Wires body needs a logged-in profile", "X needs
`X_API_BEARER_TOKEN`"). The limitation only affects real-data extraction at
runtime, not your ability to edit code or ship features.

- Preserve the fail-closed behavior for paywalled Pirate Wires; never fabricate
  body text to paper over a missing session.
- Keep the public vs authenticated code paths separate; do not require a token
  or profile for public sources.
- Do not add an X scraping fallback (see `AGENTS.md`).
